1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:01,780
Yaaawn.

2
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:02,870
Do you hear that sound?

3
00:00:04,360 --> 00:00:04,760
Aw!

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:07,060
Two spellings make it.

5
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,240
Au, and aw.

6
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:10,900
Say it with me.

7
00:00:11,820 --> 00:00:12,400
Aw!

8
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:14,750
You hear it in author.

9
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:17,650
And in saw.

10
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:20,780
Same sound, different spelling.

11
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:22,620
So which one do we write?

12
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:25,190
Ask the same question.

13
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:27,860
WHERE is the sound in the word?

14
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:31,060
Au likes the beginning and the middle.

15
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:32,660
Never the end.

16
00:00:33,340 --> 00:00:33,840
Listen.

17
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:36,340
Au-tumn.

18
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:38,140
S-au-ce.

19
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:40,440
P-au-se.

20
00:00:41,540 --> 00:00:43,900
Au stays tucked inside the word.

21
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:46,940
Aw takes the END of the word.

22
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:49,080
S-aw.

23
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:51,560
P-aw.

24
00:00:52,440 --> 00:00:53,980
Dr-aw.

25
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:55,900
Nothing comes after it.

26
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:58,680
And aw does one more job.

27
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:02,060
It sits right before a final letter too.

28
00:01:03,020 --> 00:01:03,740
Y-aw-n.

29
00:01:04,700 --> 00:01:06,420
D-aw-n.

30
00:01:07,240 --> 00:01:09,020
Cr-aw-l.

31
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:10,340
See?

32
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:12,880
The aw is still almost last.

33
00:01:13,580 --> 00:01:15,320
So we never write sau.

34
00:01:16,420 --> 00:01:18,160
And we never write awtumn.

35
00:01:19,700 --> 00:01:20,640
Au inside.

36
00:01:21,360 --> 00:01:22,600
Aw at the end.

37
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:24,410
Now here's some good news.

38
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:27,900
Remember ow, with its two different sounds?

39
00:01:28,740 --> 00:01:30,530
Aw is not like that.

40
00:01:31,320 --> 00:01:34,050
Aw only ever says one sound.

41
00:01:34,540 --> 00:01:34,940
Aw.

42
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:36,840
Always aw.

43
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:40,240
You can trust it every single time.

44
00:01:40,720 --> 00:01:41,470
Let's see them.

45
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:42,960
Author.

46
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:44,740
Autumn.

47
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:46,220
Sauce.

48
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:48,200
Launch.

49
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:50,260
Pause.

50
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:52,180
Because.

51
00:01:53,620 --> 00:01:55,460
Every one has au inside.

52
00:01:56,540 --> 00:01:57,580
Now the aw words.

53
00:01:59,020 --> 00:01:59,280
Saw.

54
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:01,280
Paw.

55
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:03,220
Draw.

56
00:02:04,520 --> 00:02:05,180
Yawn.

57
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:07,220
Dawn.

58
00:02:08,640 --> 00:02:09,240
Crawl.

59
00:02:10,340 --> 00:02:13,680
Aw at the end, or right before the final letter.

60
00:02:14,620 --> 00:02:15,420
Your turn!

61
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:17,060
Here's the word.

62
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:18,580
Yawn.

63
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:21,300
Is it au, or aw?

64
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:23,780
It's aw!

65
00:02:24,220 --> 00:02:27,640
Because aw can sit right before a final n.

66
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:29,860
So remember.

67
00:02:29,860 --> 00:02:32,200
Au sleeps inside the word.

68
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:36,080
Aw stays at the end, or right before the last letter.

69
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:37,910
Ready for the next sound?

70
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:41,520
Open the English Learning app and keep going.

71
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:42,780
It's free!
